-- Bring each existing concept to three sequence questions without changing prior data.
INSERT INTO questions (prompt, question_type, options, correct_order, explanation, concept_id)
SELECT seed.prompt, 'SEQUENCE', seed.options::jsonb, seed.ordering::jsonb, seed.explanation, c.id
FROM (VALUES
    ('A UNIX child successfully replaces its image with exec, runs the new program, and exits normally. Order these events within the child, starting with its return from fork.',
     '{"a":"The replacement program executes","b":"fork returns zero in the child","c":"The replacement program exits","d":"exec successfully replaces the child program image"}',
     '["b","d","a","c"]',
     'The child first returns from fork, calls exec to replace its image, executes the replacement program, and finally exits. A successful exec does not return to the old program.', 'Processes'),
    ('For a synchronous system call that completes without blocking or interruption, order the application and kernel events.',
     '{"a":"The kernel handles the requested service","b":"The application resumes after the system call","c":"The application executes the system-call instruction","d":"Control transfers to the kernel entry handler"}',
     '["c","d","a","b"]',
     'The application invokes the system call, control enters the kernel, the kernel handles the request, and control returns to the application.', 'Processes'),
    ('A main thread starts a worker, which computes a result and terminates. Main reads the result only after join returns successfully. Order these events.',
     '{"a":"Main reads the completed result","b":"The worker finishes computing and terminates","c":"Main creates the worker","d":"Main successfully returns from joining the worker"}',
     '["c","b","d","a"]',
     'Creation precedes worker execution. A successful join returns after termination, allowing main to read the completed result. Main may call join earlier, but its return must follow termination.', 'Threads'),
    ('A FIFO worker pool has exactly one worker, and tasks A then B are already queued. Each task runs to completion before another is dequeued. Order the worker actions.',
     '{"a":"Dequeue task B","b":"Run task A to completion","c":"Run task B to completion","d":"Dequeue task A"}',
     '["d","b","a","c"]',
     'With one worker and FIFO delivery, task A is dequeued and completed before task B is dequeued and completed.', 'Threads'),
    ('A reusable barrier requires all three workers to arrive. Worker A arrives first, B second, and C last. Order these events for this barrier phase.',
     '{"a":"Worker C arrives, satisfying the barrier participant count","b":"Worker A arrives and waits","c":"The barrier permits workers to proceed past this phase boundary","d":"Worker B arrives and waits"}',
     '["b","d","a","c"]',
     'A and B wait at the barrier. The last required arrival, C, satisfies the barrier, after which participants may proceed. Their subsequent execution order is unspecified.', 'Threads'),
    ('All four jobs arrive at time zero in FCFS queue order A, B, C, D, with positive CPU bursts and no blocking. Order their completion under nonpreemptive FCFS.',
     '{"a":"Job C completes","b":"Job A completes","c":"Job D completes","d":"Job B completes"}',
     '["b","d","a","c"]',
     'Nonpreemptive FCFS runs these ready jobs in queue order. With no blocking, completion order is A, B, C, D.', 'CPU Scheduling'),
    ('Jobs A, B, C, and D all arrive at time zero with known CPU bursts 7, 2, 5, and 1 respectively. Order their execution under nonpreemptive shortest-job-first, ignoring overhead.',
     '{"a":"Run job B (2 units)","b":"Run job A (7 units)","c":"Run job D (1 unit)","d":"Run job C (5 units)"}',
     '["c","a","d","b"]',
     'All jobs are available, and burst lengths are distinct. Shortest-job-first therefore runs D, B, C, then A.', 'CPU Scheduling'),
    ('Round-robin starts with ready queue A then B, quantum 2, and CPU bursts A=3 and B=3. There are no new arrivals or I/O waits. Order the CPU slices, ignoring switching cost.',
     '{"a":"B runs its final 1 unit and completes","b":"B runs its first 2 units","c":"A runs its first 2 units","d":"A runs its final 1 unit and completes"}',
     '["c","b","d","a"]',
     'A uses one quantum, then B uses one quantum. A then finishes its remaining unit, followed by B finishing its remaining unit.', 'CPU Scheduling'),
    ('A receiver reads one length-prefixed record from a stream. The sender has already buffered the complete record, and the receiver handles partial reads correctly. Order the receiver operations.',
     '{"a":"Read exactly the validated number of payload bytes","b":"Read the complete fixed-size length prefix","c":"Deliver the complete record to the application","d":"Decode and validate the advertised payload length"}',
     '["b","d","a","c"]',
     'The receiver first obtains the complete length prefix, validates it, collects the indicated payload bytes, and only then delivers a complete record.', 'Interprocess Communication'),
    ('A pipe writer sends a short message and closes the only write descriptor before the reader starts. Order the events through the reader reaching EOF.',
     '{"a":"The reader drains the buffered message","b":"The writer closes the only write descriptor","c":"A subsequent read returns zero bytes (EOF)","d":"The writer writes the message into the pipe buffer"}',
     '["d","b","a","c"]',
     'The message enters the buffer before the writer closes. Closing does not discard buffered bytes: the reader drains them, then a subsequent read reports EOF.', 'Interprocess Communication'),
    ('A client sends a request once over a reliable connection and waits for its reply. The server handles this request synchronously. Order this successful request-response exchange.',
     '{"a":"The server receives the request","b":"The client receives the reply","c":"The client sends the request","d":"The server processes the request and sends its reply"}',
     '["c","a","d","b"]',
     'The client sends before the server receives. The server processes the request and sends the reply before the client can receive that reply.', 'Interprocess Communication'),
    ('A thread increments a shared counter under a mutex. Order the operations so the full read-modify-write is protected.',
     '{"a":"Write the incremented value to the shared counter","b":"Release the mutex","c":"Acquire the mutex","d":"Read the shared counter into a local value"}',
     '["c","d","a","b"]',
     'The thread acquires the mutex before reading, writes the incremented value while still holding it, and releases the mutex afterward.', 'Synchronization'),
    ('In this bounded-buffer producer protocol, a producer reserves an empty slot before locking the buffer and signals an occupied slot only after unlocking. Order one production cycle.',
     '{"a":"Insert the item into the buffer","b":"Release the buffer mutex","c":"Acquire one empty-slot semaphore permit","d":"Signal the occupied-slot semaphore","e":"Acquire the buffer mutex"}',
     '["c","e","a","b","d"]',
     'This protocol reserves capacity, locks the buffer, inserts the item, unlocks, and then advertises an available item. The stated protocol fixes where signaling occurs.', 'Synchronization'),
    ('A consumer uses a condition variable for a nonempty buffer. Its first predicate check finds the buffer empty, and its wait later returns with an item available. Order these consumer events.',
     '{"a":"Recheck the predicate after wait returns with the mutex reacquired","b":"Acquire the buffer mutex","c":"Consume the item while holding the mutex","d":"Find the buffer empty and wait, atomically releasing the mutex","e":"Release the buffer mutex after consumption"}',
     '["b","d","a","c","e"]',
     'The consumer checks under the mutex, waits while empty, and rechecks after reacquiring the mutex. In this scenario the predicate is then true, so it consumes and unlocks.', 'Synchronization'),
    ('Two threads use locks L and H, with L ordered before H. Both acquire locks in increasing order and this protocol releases them in reverse order. Order one thread lock operations.',
     '{"a":"Release L","b":"Acquire H","c":"Acquire L","d":"Release H"}',
     '["c","b","d","a"]',
     'The prescribed protocol acquires L then H and releases H then L. A shared acquisition order prevents circular wait; reverse release is part of this question protocol, not a universal requirement.', 'Deadlock'),
    ('There is one resource type with one free instance. A, B, C each hold one instance and need at most 1, 2, 3 additional instances respectively to finish. No new processes arrive. Order the only safe completion sequence.',
     '{"a":"Process C obtains its remaining resources, finishes, and releases all it holds","b":"Process A obtains its remaining resources, finishes, and releases all it holds","c":"Process B obtains its remaining resources, finishes, and releases all it holds"}',
     '["b","c","a"]',
     'Only A can finish with one initially free instance; it releases its original allocation as well, leaving two free. B can then finish, leaving three free for C. This gives A, B, C.', 'Deadlock'),
    ('A system follows this recovery policy: detect a deadlock, select a victim, terminate it and reclaim its locks, then retry a previously blocked acquisition. Order these recovery stages.',
     '{"a":"Terminate the victim and reclaim its locks","b":"Retry a previously blocked acquisition using a reclaimed lock","c":"Detect the deadlocked set of threads","d":"Select a victim from the detected set"}',
     '["c","d","a","b"]',
     'Detection identifies the affected set. The policy then selects a victim, reclaims its locks through termination, and retries an acquisition. Real recovery must also address partially completed updates.', 'Deadlock'),
    ('A memory reference misses in the TLB, but its valid page is already resident. Order address translation and the resulting data access, assuming a successful page-table walk.',
     '{"a":"Combine the physical frame number with the page offset","b":"Access the data using the translated physical address","c":"Look up the virtual page in the TLB and miss","d":"Walk the page table to obtain the resident physical frame number"}',
     '["c","d","a","b"]',
     'After the TLB miss, the page-table walk supplies the frame. Combining frame and offset gives the physical address used for the data access. No disk read is required for a resident page.', 'Memory Management'),
    ('A valid disk-backed page is nonresident. A free frame is available, and the fault handler uses it without eviction. Order the demand-paging steps through successful instruction retry.',
     '{"a":"Load the page from backing storage into the allocated frame","b":"Retry the faulting instruction with the page now resident","c":"Trap to the OS on the nonresident-page access","d":"Mark the page-table mapping present after the load completes","e":"Allocate the free physical frame"}',
     '["c","e","a","d","b"]',
     'The fault traps to the OS, which allocates a free frame and loads the page. After the contents are ready, it marks the mapping present and allows the instruction to retry.', 'Memory Management'),
    ('Four resident pages A, B, C, D were last accessed at times 20, 5, 14, 9 respectively. Rank them from first to last eviction preference under exact LRU, with no intervening accesses.',
     '{"a":"Page C (last access 14)","b":"Page A (last access 20)","c":"Page D (last access 9)","d":"Page B (last access 5)"}',
     '["d","c","a","b"]',
     'LRU prefers the oldest last access. Sorting timestamps from oldest to newest gives B at 5, D at 9, C at 14, then A at 20.', 'Memory Management')
) AS seed(prompt, options, ordering, explanation, concept_name)
JOIN concepts c ON c.name = seed.concept_name;
